summary:
  A full page that lost rows to the listener's own stations ends the list.

history:
  "Show more" showed only while the rows on screen filled the cap. A page of
  fifty that held twenty-five saved stations left twenty-five rows under a
  cap of thirty, and the button went with the rest of the directory's list
  never asked for. Whether there is a next page is read from the page the
  directory sent: one that came full may have another behind it.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SearchLogic.js

find:
      return { at: n(from) + walked, more: walked < got || (size > 0 && got >= size) };

replace:
      return { at: n(from) + walked, more: walked < got };

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_searchlogic.qml::test_a_full_page_half_saved_still_has_a_next_one
  and tests/qml/tst_searchlogic.qml::test_a_page_of_nothing_but_duplicates_is_asked_past.
  Line-neutral.
